From: TDVP Feed Maintainers <feed@tdvp.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: keep the plugin install directory target-relative

The cross pkg-config wrapper correctly resolves audacious.pc through its
sysroot for compiler dependencies, but its plugin_dir variable consequently
becomes an absolute host-sysroot path.  Meson appends that path to DESTDIR
when staging a target package, so Buildroot rejects the attempted install.

Use the reviewed target prefix and libdir instead.  This keeps both the
compiled plugin discovery path and the installed payload at /usr/lib/audacious
on TDVP K230.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@ if intl_found
 endif
 
 
-install_plugindir = audacious_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'plugin_dir')
+install_plugindir = join_paths(get_option('prefix'), get_option('libdir'), 'audacious')
 
 
 conf.set_quoted('INSTALL_PLUGINDIR', install_plugindir)
